From 7e8623389cb9953d42c878a0856ebf9d41145ea1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaul Lavochkin <shaul9191@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:35:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] wasm: parse registration records without folding this
 or literals

A registration record runs a module's body as a strict generator called
without a receiver. While bun-wasm parses for one
(with_bunwasm_register_parse), module-level this stays this instead of
becoming null or exports, typeof of a primitive literal and literal
(in)equality are neither folded nor reordered, assigning to a const is
left to throw at run time, and an anonymous export default function is
not given the generated default name. A new.target outside every function
is noted for the caller, which rejects it in a module and keeps it in
CommonJS. Ordinary parsing is unchanged.
---
